00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.870
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
And we're back.

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:05.250
We have ordered some cameras, so
we can all stay safely at home

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.490
and still serve you the
Lowest Latency News.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.250
I am Priyanka Vergadia,
and welcome to "This Week

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.240
in Cloud."

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.850
This week, we're talking
about Service Directory,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.230
column-level security in
BigQuery, and the new SRS Book.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.420
Service Directory is
a managed solution

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.520
that provides a
service-centric approach

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.040
to connecting to your
cloud infrastructure,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.940
from Google Cloud, to
GCP Marketplace Services,

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.850
to your own applications.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.670
It provides
real-time information

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.710
about all of your services
in a single place,

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.580
helping you publish, discover,
and connect services,

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.230
regardless of their deployment
environment or platform.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.050
The new BigQuery column-level
security controls

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.750
are designed to help
organizations govern

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.820
their data in Google Cloud.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.310
You can now define
policies on data

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.320
that differentiate
between classes,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.630
helping you meet
compliance requirements,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.240
meaning you can grant
access to a table

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:03.390
while still barring access
to any sensitive data

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.430
in that table.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:09.180
A rapid response virtual agent
is a customized contact center

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.310
AI virtual agent
that can respond

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.380
to the increased
demand for customer

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.840
support due to COVID-19.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.900
Using this template, you can
quickly build and implement

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.200
your virtual agent, providing
additional customer support

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.070
over chat, voice, and social
channels in under two weeks.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.280
Check out the short
video to get started.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.920
If you are looking for
a new book to read,

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.630
I've got you some good news.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.470
"Building Secure and Reliable
Systems" is now available.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:42.010
This book is a page-turner
of advice and experience,

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.800
and is sure to become an
essential read for anyone

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.220
responsible for the security and
reliability of their systems.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.000
If you want to read more
